#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Soft-decision IDD MIMO detection for 8x8 256-QAM, warm-started from the hard-decision
L2A Transformer (mimo_l2a_toy_5_20_2.py) and extended to a coded 5G-LDPC system.

Design (see "Soft-IDD MIMO Detection — Design Mapped onto the Hard-Decision L2A Code"):
  * Front end: 5G LDPC encoder + bit interleaver produce *coded* bits; coded bits are
    mapped to 256-QAM and sent through y = H x + n. (Fixed routine, outside learning.)
  * Detector: an across-symbol autoregressive Transformer with per-bit sigmoid heads,
    identical in spirit to the hard-decision model. It outputs a per-bit logit L_net.
  * Prior tilt (Route C): the decoder's a-priori LLR L^A is applied only at the
    Bernoulli sampling head. With this file's convention L^A = log p(b=0)/p(b=1)
    and the neural head logit = logit P(b=1), the tilted sampling logit is
    L_tilt = L_net - L^A. The prior reshapes the *sampling* distribution; the
    network parameters never take L^A as input.
  * Soft output: posterior LLR is estimated (Rao-Blackwellized) from the tilted samples;
    the extrinsic LLR L_E = L_post - L^A is returned to the decoder (prevents the bit's
    own prior from being double counted).
  * Back end: a fixed (never-trained) Sionna LDPC5GDecoder closes the IDD loop via
    extrinsic exchange. (Fixed routine, outside learning.)

Phase-1 training (this file): the a-priori LLRs are NOT produced by rolling the IDD loop;
they are synthesized from the classical consistent-Gaussian model
    L^A ~ N( (-1)^b * sigma_A^2/2 , sigma_A^2 ),  sigma_A = J^{-1}(I_A),  I_A in [0,1],
which is the ten-Brink EXIT-chart assumption and the same recipe used by DNN-TEQ. One
*tied* operator is trained over the whole I_A range and reused at every IDD iteration.
Loss = switchable: pure population BCE on coded bits, or a residual-to-hybrid
residual/BCE curriculum using policy-gradient credit for the non-differentiable
sampled residual energy.
Final metric = coded-bit BER (and post-LDPC coded/info BER for reporting).

A faithful on-policy IDD fine-tuning phase (untied per-iteration networks) is deferred.

The Sionna pieces are optional and isolated: if Sionna is unavailable, the script falls
back to an uncoded data source and a placeholder decoder so the detector and Phase-1
training still run as a smoke test. All comments are in English.
"""

